From 21f24efcbc5d41f31d2f1e072c972b2549c4456f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Gill <peter@majorsilence.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:06:40 -0230
Subject: [PATCH] link.MachO: honor -exported_symbols_list and -exported_symbol

zig cc parsed -exported_symbols_list into the wasm export-name list, which
the Mach-O linker never reads, so every defined global stayed exported.
Carry the list to the MachO linker as macho_exported_symbols (null when no
list was given; an empty list such as /dev/null exports nothing) and, as
ld64 does, make globals that do not match it private extern so they stay
out of the export trie and -x can strip them. Matching follows ld64: plain
names, '*', '?' and '[...]' wildcards; '#' comments and surrounding
whitespace in the list file are ignored. Linker-synthesized symbols are
exempt. Also accept -exported_symbol <name>.

Also keep N_PEXT on a common symbol when converting it to a definition:
convertTentativeDefinitions forced every common to global, so a
private-extern common was exported.

Not for upstream: Zig does not accept LLM-authored patches.
---
 src/Compilation.zig       |  7 +++
 src/link.zig              |  3 ++
 src/link/MachO.zig        | 94 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/link/MachO/Object.zig |  8 +++-
 src/link/MachO/file.zig   | 12 ++++-
 src/main.zig              | 17 ++++++-
 6 files changed, 137 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

